{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-reeb-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-reeb-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the categorical Reeb derivation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-categorical-reeb-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-reeb-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","reeb","derivation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalReeb.not_unique_unconstrained","text":"categorical-reeb-unique.md","leanSource":"categorical-reeb-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-reeb-unique\"></a><p>The vertical-generator and normalization axioms together fix the derivation along the vertical distribution corresponding to the free <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code>-action. The dual form is then uniquely determined by extending to the horizontal distribution via the Maurer--Cartan condition. Therefore, the categorical Reeb derivation is unique.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.5.3","page":"b/prop-categorical-reeb-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":80},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalReeb.not_unique_unconstrained","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-reeb-unique.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
